From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vendor/keyctl: use EABI syscall numbers on linux/arm

github.com/wastore/keyctl carries the syscall numbers it needs as a
per-GOARCH constant file. The linux/arm file uses the OLD ABI numbering:

    syscall_keyctl   uintptr = 9437495   // 0x900137 = 0x900000 + 311
    syscall_add_key  uintptr = 9437493   // 0x900135 = 0x900000 + 309
    syscall_setfsgid uintptr = 9437323   // 0x90008b = 0x900000 + 139

0x900000 is __NR_SYSCALL_BASE for ARM OABI. Go's linux/arm port is EABI,
where the base is 0 and the numbers are plainly 311 / 309 / 139
(arch/arm/tools/syscall.tbl). Every one of the three constants above is
exactly the right EABI number with the OABI base bolted on, so the sibling
files for 386/arm64/ppc are all correct and only this one is wrong -- it
was evidently transcribed from an OABI table.

The consequence is not a graceful ENOSYS. AzCopy caches its OAuth token in
the kernel session keyring, so EVERY `azcopy login*` subcommand goes
through here, and the bogus syscall number takes the whole process out:

    $ azcopy login status
    SIGILL: illegal instruction
    PC=0x1edf4 m=0 sigcode=4
    goroutine 1 gp=0x4804148 m=0 mp=0x27226f8 [syscall]:
    syscall.Syscall6(0x900137, 0x0, 0xfffffffd, 0x1, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0)
            syscall/syscall_linux.go:96 +0x8
    github.com/wastore/keyctl.keyctl(0x0, {0x5093a5c, 0x2, 0x2})
            github.com/wastore/keyctl@v0.3.1/sys_linux.go:114 +0x16c
    github.com/wastore/keyctl.newKeyring(0xfffffffd)

With the three constants corrected the same command answers normally:

    $ azcopy login status
    INFO: You are currently not logged in. Please login using 'azcopy login'

(Both transcripts are from the ARMv7 binary run under qemu-arm; see
docs/azcopy.md for the full test matrix and what it does and does not
prove.)

Provenance
----------
Origin:       Not upstream. Written for this repo against
              github.com/wastore/keyctl v0.3.1 as vendored by
              Azure/azure-storage-azcopy v10.32.7.
Author:       Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Upstream:     NO -- not submitted, to either wastore/keyctl (the fork
              AzCopy depends on) or jsipprell/keyctl (the parent it was
              forked from; the same OABI constants are in both). Both
              repos have been dormant for years. Worth sending; not sent.
Disposition:  RUNTIME BLOCKER for the `login` command family. Not a build
              blocker -- the package compiles and every non-login
              subcommand works without it -- so it must NOT be dropped
              silently on a version bump on the grounds that "the build is
              green". A green build proves nothing about this patch.
Patches WHAT: vendor/, not the AzCopy sources. That directory does not
              exist in the upstream GitHub archive; it is created by
              Buildroot's own Go download post-process
              (support/download/go-post-process, which runs `go mod
              vendor`) and is therefore part of the -go2 tarball this
              package pins the hash of. So the file IS present at
              .stamp_patched time, and the hash pin is what makes the
              content it patches deterministic. If a future keyctl bump
              changes this file, the patch fails to apply and the build
              goes red -- which is the desired failure mode.
Scope:        linux/arm only. sys_linux_386.go, sys_linux_arm64.go and the
              ppc variants were read and are already correct; they are not
              touched.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 vendor/github.com/wastore/keyctl/sys_linux_arm.go | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/wastore/keyctl/sys_linux_arm.go b/vendor/github.com/wastore/keyctl/sys_linux_arm.go
index 8202b66..d004af1 100644
--- a/vendor/github.com/wastore/keyctl/sys_linux_arm.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/wastore/keyctl/sys_linux_arm.go
@@ -1,7 +1,10 @@
 package keyctl
 
+// EABI syscall numbers (arch/arm/tools/syscall.tbl). The values these
+// replaced were the same numbers with the ARM OABI __NR_SYSCALL_BASE
+// (0x900000) added, which Go's EABI-only linux/arm port cannot use.
 const (
-	syscall_keyctl   uintptr = 9437495
-	syscall_add_key  uintptr = 9437493
-	syscall_setfsgid uintptr = 9437323
-)
\ No newline at end of file
+	syscall_keyctl   uintptr = 311
+	syscall_add_key  uintptr = 309
+	syscall_setfsgid uintptr = 139
+)
-- 
2.51.0

